#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317393 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166960 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9dcbb0-d943-5340-916e-d789b6ab03bc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Value to What a Fourier Series Converges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0037eb03-213e-5d10-a8b1-2c3b156f0fd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0037eb03-213e-5d10-a8b1-2c3b156f0fd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315114} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab6fb759-4189-56fa-94b4-4e7de6084501" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "97ff3547-7e44-5c45-a91b-58643d43344d" :question/math-academy-id "q-343364" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+2}, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ 1, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. Find the value to which the Fourier series of the $4$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ converges when $x=-2.$\n\nThe Fourier series converges to {{field-1}} when $x=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a $2L$-periodic piecewise smooth function with the corresponding Fourier series\n\n$$\nS(x)=\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x).\n$$\n\nThen, the series converges for all $x\\in R.$\n\n- If $f(x)$ is continuous at $x,$ then the series converges to the value of the function at this point:\n\n$$\nS(x)=f(x)\n$$\n\n- If $f(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x,$ then the series converges to the midpoint between the values of left- and right-sided limits of the function at this point:\n\n$$\nS(x)=\\frac{{f}^{-}(x)+{f}^{+}(x)}{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{-}(x)$ and ${f}^{+}(x)$ are the left- and right-sided limits of the function at this point, respectively.\n\nNotice that the $4$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of our function $F(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-2.$ The one-sided limits at this point are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-}(-2) & ={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{-}}f(x)=1 \\\\ {f}^{+}(-2) & ={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}f(x)={e}^{-2+2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ converges to \n\n$$\n\\frac{{f}^{-}(-2)+{f}^{+}(-2)}{2}=\\frac{1+1}{2}=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375031 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166960 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9dcbb0-d943-5340-916e-d789b6ab03bc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Value to What a Fourier Series Converges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dcce98c-8760-56f2-b17b-5fd945b150e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dcce98c-8760-56f2-b17b-5fd945b150e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375033} :answer-field/id #uuid "948a4c6b-6866-5b53-840b-620e511c4ece" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375032}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae903844-3154-5fe9-a420-6a9e8272ce91" :question/math-academy-id "q-343366" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-26, & x\\in [-5,0) \\\\ -3x, & x\\in [0,5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. Find the value to which the Fourier series of the $10$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ converges when $x=5.$\n\nThe Fourier series converges to {{field-1}} when $x=5.$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a $2L$-periodic piecewise smooth function with the corresponding Fourier series\n\n$$\nS(x)=\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x).\n$$\n\nThen, the series converges for all $x\\in R.$\n\n- If $f(x)$ is continuous at $x,$ then the series converges to the value of the function at this point:\n\n$$\nS(x)=f(x)\n$$\n\n- If $f(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x,$ then the series converges to the midpoint between the values of left- and right-sided limits of the function at this point:\n\n$$\nS(x)=\\frac{{f}^{-}(x)+{f}^{+}(x)}{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{-}(x)$ and ${f}^{+}(x)$ are the left- and right-sided limits of the function at this point, respectively.\n\nNotice that the $10$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of our function $F(x)$ is not continuous at $x=5.$ The one-sided limits at this point are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-}(5) & ={lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}f(x)=-3(5)=-15 \\\\ {f}^{+}(5) & ={lim}_{x\\to {5}^{+}}f(x)={5}^{2}-26=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ converges to \n\n$$\n\\frac{{f}^{-}(5)+{f}^{+}(5)}{2}=\\frac{-15+(-1)}{2}=-8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432958 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166960 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9dcbb0-d943-5340-916e-d789b6ab03bc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Value to What a Fourier Series Converges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54b97394-ead1-526b-8c32-cf56b7a9ff77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54b97394-ead1-526b-8c32-cf56b7a9ff77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432914} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd811455-ce81-5be1-8d33-3a112d11cc83" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7b12d98f-f620-5c11-959f-ef743de24735" :question/math-academy-id "q-343386" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x, & x\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0] \\\\ {e}^{x}, & x\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. Find the value to which the Fourier series of the $\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is converging when $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\nThe Fourier series converges to {{field-1}} when $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a $2L$-periodic piecewise smooth function with the corresponding Fourier series\n\n$$\nS(x)=\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x).\n$$\n\nThen, the series converges for all $x\\in R.$\n\n- If $f(x)$ is continuous at $x,$ then the series converges to the value of the function at this point:\n\n$$\nS(x)=f(x)\n$$\n\n- If $f(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x,$ then the series converges to the midpoint between the values of left- and right-sided limits of the function at this point:\n\n$$\nS(x)=\\frac{{f}^{-}(x)+{f}^{+}(x)}{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{-}(x)$ and ${f}^{+}(x)$ are the left- and right-sided limits of the function at this point, respectively.\n\nNotice that the $\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of our function $F(x)$ is continuous at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ converges to \n\n$$\nf\\,(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})=cos\\,(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420495 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166961 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3cb7656-1ce6-5b6a-9e88-5ba24a943c3f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Infinite Sum Using Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cec1b04-11f1-52b4-bede-6fa1be707451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420476} {:answer/id #uuid "3233da4d-abf4-509b-8a83-199acf697664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420478} {:answer/id #uuid "56ce5d4f-b6f2-580a-8157-fe69a694922d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420479} {:answer/id #uuid "87300a85-1a3b-5482-8d6a-77042fc3955d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3233da4d-abf4-509b-8a83-199acf697664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420478} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a2d1532-e62f-56cf-ad90-cfb160e1a05b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420490} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09eccf47-a4e8-5569-a8eb-3f4ce0ab918c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420471} {:answer/id #uuid "c8c2a375-3ff9-5e2d-be12-112ac4c6827d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "discontinuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09eccf47-a4e8-5569-a8eb-3f4ce0ab918c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 1