t :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402348} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71109050-5463-5ad1-a2e0-992ca3f99166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402354} {:answer/id #uuid "bc720c6e-5092-5a46-980f-2cf9b11293e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "discontinuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71109050-5463-5ad1-a2e0-992ca3f99166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402354} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d6cd00a-0022-5089-9075-29d1a852af1f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402353}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09760520-d150-5b51-9f43-20d7cea8711d" :question/math-academy-id "q-343446" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4, & x\\in [-\\pi ,0] \\\\ -2, & x\\in (0,\\pi )\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. The Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼1-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12}{\\pi (2n-1)}sin\\,((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nAt $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nsin\\,((2n-1)\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is \n{{field-2}}\nat $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1}={{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite our Fourier series as\n\n$$\nf(x)∼1-\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot sin\\,((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nsin\\,((2n-1)\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})=sin\\,(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi )=(-1)^{n+1}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is $\\text{continuous}$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=-2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =1-\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot sin\\,((2n-1)\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\ -2 & =1-\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot (-1)^{n+1} \\\\ -3 & =-\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
